      "title": "Resolving Duplicate Accounts During Bulk Import (SSO Integration Module)",
      "content_summary": "Addresses issues where bulk user imports via the SSO Integration Module result in duplicate accounts or partial failures, typically caused by upstream dependency mismatches or operator input errors.",
      "content_body": "When bulk imports stall or create duplicates, first verify that the identity source (Session Controller) is synchronizing correctly before retrying the import. Partial failures often stem from malformed CSV fields or conflicting existing records, requiring an access review to identify operator errors. If the provisioning queue remains stuck, check for dependency timeouts on the SSO gateway and engage the vendor if logs show persistent API 429 or 500 errors. Always re-run failed batches in isolated chunks after correcting the initial data anomalies."
